 ## 2026-09-02
 
+### 1900 — An absent clause has nothing to mutate, and the artifact row read as if it were there
+
+- FINDING: `validateManifestEntries` enforced the duplicate and destination-case-collision halves of SPEC.md:4768-4769 and dropped the OVERLAPPING half entirely. On checkpoint `a031128` a manifest declaring file `a` with file `a/b`, symlink `s` with file `s/x`, or file `a` with directory `a/b` was ACCEPTED at both identity entries. A symlink parent over a real child is a materialization-escape primitive, so this was a path-safety hole on landed main.
+- ROOT CAUSE of why every existing gate stayed green: mutation testing cannot surface an ABSENT clause. There is no operator to rewrite, no literal to shift, no guard to delete. The 47-call-site vocabulary sweep, the derived refusal-coverage gate, the declared-bounds inventory and five seeded fuzz corpora were all satisfied by a validator missing a third of one normative sentence. It was found by reading the spec sentence against the code, which is the only method that finds a clause that is not there.
+- FINDING: `testdata/constraint-enumeration.md` actively hid it. The row narrowed "overlapping" to the external child-partition case and dispositioned the entry-local half as "duplicate/case collision is enforced", so the sentence read as fully accounted for. An enumeration row that paraphrases half a clause is worse than a missing row: a missing row fails the inventory, a half-quoted one passes review. The row now quotes the whole sentence and states that all three properties are entry-local.
+- DECISION: detection reuses the strict bytewise order the same loop already proves instead of re-deriving each path's ancestor set. Every ancestor is a proper prefix ending at `/`, so it precedes its descendants and the open non-directory owners form a stack.
+- FINDING, the non-obvious half: an owner may be closed only once the scan passes strictly above `owner + "/"`, not on the first non-descendant path. `.` (0x2E) sorts below `/` (0x2F), so `a.txt` sits between `a` and `a/b`; the naive closing rule evicts the `a` owner before its escaping child arrives and admits the overlap. Mutant M5 is exactly that implementation and needed its own three-entry case to die.
+- DECISION, an over-refusal declined: parent directories are NOT required to be declared. SPEC.md §10.4/§13.14 states no such rule, and the shipped `transferManifestWithEntries(count)` fixture already declares `p/00000` with no `p` entry. Overlap is also compared bytewise, not case-folded — folding does not preserve byte order, so the stack cannot run over folded paths — and that narrowing is disclosed in the artifact row rather than silently assumed.
+- EVIDENCE: 7 mutants, 7 killed, 0 survivors, every acceptance case green throughout. Two of them are the pair that proves no tag arm is redundant: restricting the refusal to `file` owners kills only the symlink and hardlink cases, restricting it to non-`file` owners kills only the rest. `BUG-260902-2luo5h_overlap-mutants.log`.
+- SCOPE: `README.md`, `internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/clause_refusal_test.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/boundary_constraints_test.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md`
+- STATUS: BUG-260902-2luo5h on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-1evi33`, one commit past checkpoint `a031128`; `internal/canonicaljson` coverage 97.2% (measured at the checkpoint in a throwaway worktree) -> 97.2%; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l .`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-cover`, all five seeded fuzz targets, `tracecheck` and `cataloggen -check` exit 0; handed off to review.
+
 ### 1810 — Two derived counts collided in one merge, and only one of them was honest
 
 - FINDING: reapplying the record-schema Story onto trunk `10aaa16` produced nine conflict blocks, not the four structural hunks the previous probe recorded. The extra five were derived counts that both sides had bumped independently: `AcceptanceCases` in `traceability_test.go`, the two `acceptance_cases=` strings in `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, and the count sentence plus tools row in `README.md`. A count conflict cannot be resolved by choosing a side; base 29 + trunk 6 + accepted 3 = 38, which the union-merged registry then confirmed at `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` (`acceptance_cases=38`).
